.TH GGUF_INSPECT 1 "2026-06-29" "Symoneural" "Symoneural Helper Utilities"
.SH NAME
gguf_inspect \- GGUF file metadata reader and patcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python helpers/python/gguf_inspect.py
.B read
.I path
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR KEY ]
.RB [ \-\-tensors ]
.PP
.B python helpers/python/gguf_inspect.py
.B patch
.I path
.I output
.I patches
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gguf_inspect.py
provides sub-commands to read or modify GGUF file metadata.
The
.B read
sub-command prints metadata KV pairs or tensor descriptors as JSON.
The
.B patch
sub-command copies a GGUF file and applies JSON-specified metadata updates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B read \fIpath\fR [\-\-key \fIKEY\fR] [\-\-tensors]
Read metadata from
.IR path .
Without options, all KV metadata is printed as JSON.
With
.B \-\-key
.IR KEY ,
only the value for that key is printed.
With
.BR \-\-tensors ,
tensor descriptors (name, shape, type, n_elements, data_offset) are printed instead.
.TP
.B patch \fIsrc\fR \fIdst\fR \fIpatches\fR
Copy
.I src
to
.I dst
and apply
.I patches
(a JSON object string) to the metadata.
Only string and numeric scalar patches are supported; tensor data is copied verbatim.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Read all metadata:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/gguf_inspect.py read model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Read a single key:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/gguf_inspect.py read model.gguf \-\-key general.architecture
.EE
.RE
.PP
List tensors:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/gguf_inspect.py read model.gguf \-\-tensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Patch metadata:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/gguf_inspect.py patch model.gguf patched.gguf '{"general.name":"MyModel"}'
.EE
.RE
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B gguf
(pip install gguf).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tensor_utils (1),
.BR quant_utils (1)
